{"reviewedAt":"2026-10-16","jurisdiction":"Texas","scope":"62 catalog career entry requirements; standard domestic first-entry routes, with protected-title and regulated-scope distinctions.","method":"Primary regulator pages, statutes, occupation preparation sources, and Texas business permit inventory. No unsupported universal degree/licensure minimum is inferred. Ordinary-duty absence findings are editorial inventory reviews, marked moderate confidence, rather than legal clearance for every specialized service.","coverage":{"careers":62,"sourced":40,"inventoryReviewed":22},"importantDistinctions":["Texas dietetics is a protected-title act. Nutritionist/Dietitian alone does not require an LD license. New RDN eligibility has a separate graduate-degree rule.","Tattoo studios/temporary locations are licensed. Texas DSHS does not issue a separate individual tattoo artist license; aseptic/infection-prevention competence remains required.","Texas CPA certification added the 120-credit/two-year pathway effective August 1, 2026. The 150-credit/one-year pathway remains. Specific coursework/exam/ethics conditions also apply.","ACR registered technician minimum age is 16; under-18 direct supervision applies. An older TDLR FAQ contains an outdated age-18 statement, so the specific 2023 update and Oct 2025 application take precedence.","Engineering and public geoscience licensure depend on regulated work scope and statutory exemptions. A license is not mandatory for every employee with the occupation title.","General paralegal duties are distinct from licensed legal paraprofessional and attorney authority.","Sonography uses non-ionizing ultrasound. Medical radiologic certification does not establish a sonographer license.","School librarian requirements differ from general public/academic librarian employment."],"limitations":["Not an exhaustive personal application checklist: identity, fees, citizenship/lawful-presence rules, criminal-history review, renewal, foreign-degree eq